Issue #564 (root is never woken) - FROZEN CONTRACT for the two lanes. Read root-wake/lane-a or root-wake/lane-b for your assignment.

DEFECTS (operator, 2026-09-23T03:35Z): (1) delivery - docs/54 section 4.2 assumed MCP notifications wake the root; an idle session reads them only inside a turn something else started. (2) addressing - no wake class means "this is waiting on you". Operator scope addition: delivery must work for EVERY supported harness (claude-code, codex, omp incl. Kimi, grok, kimi-code, muse), each with its own verified turn-starting path; where a harness cannot be woken the deployment must say so up front (doctor + deployment view), never discover it by silence.

FROZEN MODULE INTERFACE - lane A creates impl/src/root-wake.mjs exporting exactly:
  export const ROOT_WAKE_HARNESSES = Object.freeze(['claude-code','codex','omp','grok','kimi-code','muse']);
  export function rootWakeChannel(harness) -> row | null;   // row = {harness, channel, wakeable, mechanism, evidence, note}
  export function rootWakeTable() -> Object.freeze([row...]) // one row per ROOT_WAKE_HARNESSES entry, table order
  export function rootWakeTurnStart(harness, { sessionRef, frameText }) -> {command, args} | null;
  export function normalizeRootWakeTarget(value) -> {harness, sessionRef} | null;  // config declaration validation
  export async function deliverRootWake({ target, frame }, seams = {}) -> {
    ok: boolean, harness, channel, reason, receipt: {sentAt, sent} | null }
  // reason is CLOSED: 'delivered' | 'no_target' | 'unknown_harness' | 'no_turn_starting_channel'
  //                     | 'session_running' | 'spawn_failed'
  // seams = { spawn, socketWrite, now } - tests inject fakes; production defaults are spawn+node:net
Lane B imports this module; nothing else in the deployment may opencode a per-harness wake command.

TURN-STARTING EVIDENCE (verified by help text on this host, 2026-09-23; do not re-derive):
- claude-code: 'claude --resume <session-id> -p <text>' continues that session ("--resume <session-id>, continues that session in the background under the same ID, or starts a copy and says so when the session is already running"). Binary at ~/.local/bin/claude.
- codex: 'codex exec resume <session-id> <prompt>' ('resume  Resume a previous session by id or pick the most recent with --last' under codex exec). The shared local app-server daemon (codex app-server, codex agents) is the longer-term channel; the CLI resume is the verified one today.
- omp: 'omp -r <session> -p <text>' (-r/--resume, -p/--print; --mode=rpc is the protocol impl/src/omp-rpc.mjs speaks).
- grok: the ACP session adapter (impl/src/grok-acp.mjs, cmd default 'grok', 'grok agent stdio' JSON-RPC/NDJSON): session/prompt starts a turn on an existing session.
- kimi-code: the ACP session adapter (impl/src/kimi-acp.mjs, cmd default 'kimi', kimi ... acp): session/prompt starts a turn.
- muse: 'muse exec [--prompt-file]' headless and 'muse resume <session-ref>' (binary ~/.local/bin/muse).
- claude-code ALSO has a live cross-session socket channel: /tmp/cc-socks/<pid>.sock (sockets observed on this host; a peer wrote to one and recorded {"sent": <uuid>, "target": "uds:/tmp/cc-socks/<pid>.sock", "target_pid": <pid>, "delivery": "written_to_socket"}). The frame shape is Claude Code-internal and UNVERIFIED from Baton: report that in the row's note, do not make it the default channel, and never write to a socket a test did not inject.

HONESTY RULE: a channel is either verified (evidence names the command/flag or the adapter file) or the row says wakeable:false with the reason. Never fake a mechanism. Where no target is declared, delivery reports no_target and the deployment reports it up front.

DELIVERY ONCE PER ITEM: one durable swarm.root_waiting row per owed item (lane B), one delivery record per item (Lane B records the outcome; a second attempt for the same item does not happen). The once rule is enforced by reading existing rows, never a clock (#163).

TESTS AND HOST: targeted test files only, run with 'node --test <file>' from impl/ (or 'node scripts/run-suite.mjs <file>' when you want the deployment's expected-red judgment). NEVER npm test or the full suite (16 GB host, #561). Landings are blocked deployment-wide (publish remote undeclared) - publish your contribution, do not attempt to land.

CONTRIBUTION SHAPE: closed contract (subject, base{observedHead,rebasedOnto}, commit{sha,branch}, items[{id,status,change,files,test,evidence}], verification{targeted,gates,fullSuite,environmentRed}, carriedForward, needsFromOthers). Publish with: cat payload.json | node "$BATON_SWARM_CLIENT" swarm.update -
